            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Monica"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for an xmas app and it was a big hit! I only rated it a 4 because i did make a couple minor changes. I added a few Tbsp of the pickle juice and a couple large dallops of sourcream to make it creamier! Will be making it again for sure!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BRAA1957"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great dip, have made it many times but have started using 1 small jar dill pickle relish instead of dicing pickles myself. I drain some of the juice off and add back as needed.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-15T17:38:55.346Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mego"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Been making this for many years. 1pkg cream cheese, 1 pkg. dried beef, 1/4 of a Clausen pickle. Variation I'd replace the pickle with sliced green onion and a couple dashed of worcestershire sauce. Both are a hit.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-15T15:56:39.753Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carrie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is totally different from the one I grew up on &amp; we didn't put pressed beef in the dip with pickles. How I was taught 1 cream cheese soften, 1 sour cream, chopped white onion, chopped Milwaukee Pickles add pepper &amp; garlic salt to your tasting mix all together let it chill in refrigerator and you can put the pressed beef in same dip bas minus the pickles. A lot better this way &amp; not so thick",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-08T23:42:38.403Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ann Brown"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for our family Christmas gathering and it was a huge hit. I made some additions to the dip. I added a few spoons of sour cream and a small amount of mayo. Instead of using beef I used ham. This tasted like dill pickle roll ups without having to spread the cream cheese on the pickle and roll the ham around it.",
            "datePublished": "2017-12-28T02:32:54.727Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "OZBOZ79"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! I find it's easier to use a jar of dill pickle relish (don't drain it!). It doesn't *look* pretty but boy does it taste good. Everyone loves it!",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-04T19:38:22.400Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BrightOrzo5287"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think it was great. I did make a couple changes though. I make this with diced olives, bell pepper and onion with the dried beef and cream cheese. Also added dill weed. YUM! I use this as a spread with crackers instead of a dip.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-15T15:55:35.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan Priem"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’ve made pickle dip for many years. I had some people be skeptical but once they tried it I’ve never had anything but 5 star rating from people. They are always amazed at how easy it is. The beef chips are new to me. We just mixed cream cheese, diced pickles with a little juice, and a teaspoon of garlic salt. Yum.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-15T17:19:46.801Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JovialStock4858"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this quite often, I use 1/2 cream cheese 1/2 sour cream. I also add a little season salt to give it more flavor. Dried beef has more flavor but regular thin sliced beef works to. Always a big hit when I don't have time for pickle wraps.",
            "datePublished": "2022-04-21T15:23:49.574Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sue Ann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was SO good and easy. I followed a couple reviews and used 8 oz whipped cream cheese and also used about two-thirds of a small jar of dill pickle relish in lieu of pickle spears. It's ready to eat right away. Served with crackers.",
            "datePublished": "2017-09-17T22:23:16.420Z"
          },
