              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "teddygrace"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband's family are dill pickle (as well as peanut) fanatics so I once made a dill pickle dip but it didn't include the dried beef. The dill flavor in that one was almost too strong but the dried beef in this one fixed that issue. I suppose you could drain &amp; use dill relish but I really like the way the chopped pickles look. I cut them into cubes where possible - but first I cut the pickles lengthwise &amp; scooped out the seeds. Looking forward to making this again soon.",
